within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.B_BloodAndBloodFormingOrgans.B01A_AntithromboticAgents.B01AE03_Argatroban;
model Argatroban_Akimoto2011_PD_act
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Akimoto_2011 :: ACT (activated clotting time)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 116,      // [s; s × 1]
    Emax = 516,  // [s; s × 1]
    EC50 = 0.0041,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 0.87,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 41000, Interval = 82),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Argatroban_Akimoto2011_PD_act</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Akimoto K et al., <i>Journal of clinical pharmacology 51(6):805–818</i> 2011 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1177/0091270010372627\">doi:10.1177/0091270010372627</a>) — activated clotting time [s] against argatroban ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        116 s        drug-free response (baseline) (Baseline, Q324)
  Emax  =        516 s        maximal effect term (E max, Q320)
  EC50  =       4100 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC 50, Q321)
  gamma =       0.87          Hill coefficient (Hill constant, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of argatroban per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 116   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (4100 ng/mL)  response 374
  exposure -> infinity  response 632</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Akimoto_2011: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Argatroban_Akimoto2011_PD_act;
